This includes, without limitation:

- selling the software, or selling a product or service whose value derives substantially from it;
- bundling it into a paid product, a paid service, or a paid support plan;
- running it as part of a hosted or managed service for which you charge;
- using it to advertise, promote or drive traffic to a commercial offering;
- placing it behind a paywall, an ad network, or a subscription.

### 2.2 Distribution terms travel with the software

If you distribute this software or a modified version, you must:

- include this license, unmodified, in the distribution;
- keep the copyright notice in Section 1 above;
- apply this same license to your modified version — you may not relicense it, and you may not add
